IO-K8s 1.106 added `IO::K8s::Apimachinery::Pkg::Apis::Meta::V1::APIGroupList` and `::APIResourceList` as real classes (Changes, 1.106 section; lib/IO/K8s/Apimachinery/Pkg/Apis/Meta/V1/APIGroupList.pm). The sibling dist IO-K8s-Deprecated 1.105, released five days earlier, ships tombstones under exactly these two names that `die` on load (~/dev/io-k8s-p5-deprecated/lib/IO/K8s/Apimachinery/Pkg/Apis/Meta/V1/APIGroupList.pm:9). Both dists install the same file path, so whoever installs IO-K8s-Deprecated after IO-K8s replaces the working discovery classes with stubs.

The fix belongs in io-k8s-p5-deprecated (remove the two stubs, see the finding there); this card is the IO-K8s side: decide it together and add a guard so it cannot recur - e.g. a maint check or author test that fails when a module path in lib/ also exists in ../io-k8s-p5-deprecated/lib.

Done when: no module name is shipped by both dists, and a check on one of the two sides enforces it.

